-- A TYPICALLY on a computed field, one with a MEANS clause, is an error
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md T1). The field's value always comes from its
-- MEANS expression, so a default could never be taken. It used to be accepted as
-- metadata that did nothing; now that a TYPICALLY on any other field is a
-- default a construction takes, the exception is refused.

DECLARE Widget HAS
  price IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 10
  taxed IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 11
    MEANS price * 1.09
  total IS A NUMBER
    MEANS taxed + 1
